## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design secure, multi-tenant data architectures with proper cryptographic isolation, cross-account access patterns, and safe deployment practices for sensitive analytics workloads.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant KMS CMK isolation with restrictive key policies
- Cross-account access using STS AssumeRole
- Tenant-specific masking rule storage and retrieval
- Blue-green deployments and canary testing for safe rollouts

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "Allow central analytics plane decrypt",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::CENTRAL_ACCOUNT_ID:role/AnalyticsPlaneRole"
      },
      "Action": [
        "kms:Decrypt",
        "kms:DescribeKey"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kms:*:TENANT_ACCOUNT_ID:key/*",
      "Condition": {
        "ArnLike": {
          "kms:EncryptionContext:TenantId": "arn:aws:kms:*:TENANT_ACCOUNT_ID:key/CMK_ID"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

The key policy uses the `kms:EncryptionContext` condition to ensure the central plane can only decrypt data encrypted under the specific tenant's CMK, preventing cross-tenant data access.

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of cross‑account access, least privilege, and data isolation in S3 with AWS IAM roles and bucket policies. It also touches on revocation and testing in a real-world partner scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Cross‑account IAM trust and role policies
- S3 bucket policies and per‑prefix access
- Least privilege and access revocation
- Private access options (VPC endpoint) and public access controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Trust policy (role in data account)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::<PartnerAcct>:root"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```

```javascript
// Role policy: s3:GetObject on partner prefix
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-bucket/partner-prefix/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

```javascript
// Bucket policy: allow role to read
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::<DataAcct>:role/PartnerReadRole"},
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-bucket/partner-prefix/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

